{"id":"aero_uvw_field_noise","compound_name":"Simulation::Aero::aero_uvw_field_noise","source_path":"aero_uvw_field_noise/aero_uvw_field_noise.json","category":"Smoke","author":"Autodesk","description":"Using uvw texture coordinates with fields to apply noise to aero fog density.","documentation_file":"aero_uvw_field_noise_docs_ENU.md","documentation":"## Aero fog noise through fields and UVWs\n\n### What it does\n\nThis graph adds post-simulation noise to `fog_density` using fields, making use of two sets of UVW texture coordinates that are advected with an aero simulation and periodically updated. This technique adds detail with minimal computational cost.  \n\n### Inputs and outputs\n\nInputs for this graph are the meshes which act as sources for an aero simulation. The output is the resulting aero simulation volume with noise applied to `fog_density`.  \n\n### How it works\n\n- Blue section: Here the `aero_uvw_settings` node advects 2 sets of uvw texture coordinates with the aero simulation. The coordinates are reset every 1.5 seconds with an offset of 0.75 seconds (`offset_ratio` * `period`). The given name is simply \"uvw\" which means the sets emerge from the solver as `voxel_uvw1` and `voxel_uvw2`.  The weight for each set of coordinates also accompany the data as `voxel_uvw1_weight` and `voxel_uvw2_weight` respectively.  \n\n- Purple section: In this section, the uvw texture coordinates are retrieved from the output of the aero solver and those positions are used to sample two fractal noisefields. By multiplying each noise field with its associated coordinate weight and adding the two together, the two noise textures fade in and out in an alternating fashion (determined by the `aero_uvw_settings`) which gives the illusion of continuity and while avoiding stretching.\n\n- Orange section: Finally, the noise textures from the previous section are applied to the aero `fog_density`. This is done by extracting `fog_density`, multiplying it by the resulting texture, and then setting it back.","library_dependencies":{"Amino":"2.15.0.9","bif":"2.15.0.9","fields":"2.15.0.9","fluids":"2.15.0.9","geometries":"2.15.0.9"},"graph_ports":[{"portName":"out_geometry2","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"}],"terminal_states":[{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::final","enabled":"false"},{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::proxy","enabled":"false"},{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::diagnostic","enabled":"false"}],"counts":{"nodes":32,"connections":38,"values":75,"compounds":2},"node_types":{"Core::Graph::pass":5,"Core::Math::multiply":3,"Modeling::Primitive::create_mesh_sphere":3,"Core::Fields::fractal_noise_field":2,"Geometry::Properties::get_geo_property":2,"Core::Fields::sample_field":2,"Core::Object::get_property":2,"Simulation::Aero::aero_uvw_settings":1,"Core::Math::add":1,"Core::Time::time":1,"Core::Fields::scalar_field":1,"Simulation::Aero::source_air":1,"Simulation::Aero::aero_solver_settings":1,"spheres":1,"Simulation::Aero::simulate_aero":1,"Rendering::Materials::assign_material":1,"Rendering::Arnold::Arnold_standard_volume_mat":1,"Geometry::Properties::get_voxel_fog_density":1,"Geometry::Properties::set_voxel_fog_density":1,"Modeling::Common::merge_geometry":1},"edge_type_pairs":{"Simulation::Aero::simulate_aero -> Core::Graph::pass":3,"Modeling::Primitive::create_mesh_sphere -> Modeling::Common::merge_geometry":3,"Core::Fields::fractal_noise_field -> Core::Fields::sample_field":2,"Geometry::Properties::get_geo_property -> Core::Fields::sample_field":2,"Core::Fields::sample_field -> Core::Math::multiply":2,"Core::Object::get_property -> Core::Math::multiply":2,"Core::Math::multiply -> Core::Math::add":2,"Core::Fields::scalar_field -> Core::Fields::fractal_noise_field":2,"Core::Graph::pass -> Core::Graph::pass":2,"Core::Graph::pass -> Core::Object::get_property":2,"Core::Graph::pass -> Geometry::Properties::get_geo_property":2,"Core::Math::add -> Core::Math::multiply":1,"Core::Time::time -> Core::Fields::scalar_field":1,"Simulat